#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
sca - CPE camera/WiFi scanner with WiFi password disclosure.

Vendors whose WiFi key is exposed without login:
  * Realtek  -> wlsecurity_all.htm : wps_psk_old
  * Netis    -> netcore_get.cgi    : key_wpa / wsc_psk
  * Tenda    -> goform/WifiBasicGet: wifiPwd (when present)
Other vendors (TP-Link, ipTIME, ...) require login.  A best-effort login
with admin/admin is attempted before falling back to "login req.".

Connected-device counts come from:
  * Realtek -> status.htm      : clientnum / mssid_clientnum / rp_clientnum
  * Netis   -> netcore_get.cgi : dhcp_client_list (fallback: arp_list)
  * Tenda   -> goform/getWifiClientList (when the firmware exposes it)
  * anything else that needs login -> N/A

Design borrowed from the `scan` tool:
  * live streaming output (flush + print_lock)
  * fast host-alive check (TCP:80 -> ping) before any curl
  * ThreadPoolExecutor (-t/--threads, default 18)
  * live numbering (# in discovery order)

Arabic SSIDs are reshaped and ordered for a terminal without BiDi support
(QTerminal), so they read correctly on screen.

Usage:
  sca [start=175] [end=254] [-t THREADS] [-s SUBNET] [--realtek-only]
"""

